[00:00.000 --> 00:03.000]  If electrons truly have angular momentum,
[00:03.000 --> 00:07.500]  then flipping their spin should cause the entire bolt to start rotating.
[00:07.500 --> 00:14.500]  Now in an atom, an electrons mass is tiny, only about 0.03% of the total atoms mass.
[00:14.500 --> 00:18.000]  So while each electron has a lot of angular momentum,
[00:18.000 --> 00:20.500]  it has to move a huge amount of mass.
[00:20.500 --> 00:24.000]  That means that the rotation of the bolt will be very small.
[00:24.000 --> 00:26.900]  To detect it, I'll hang the bolt from a string
[00:54.000 --> 00:56.500]  and an electric current through these coils,
[01:24.000 --> 01:26.500]  flip their spin simultaneously,
[01:54.000 --> 01:56.500]  and spin.
