[00:00.000 --> 00:19.780]  The basic problem in understanding UFO propulsion is to find out how alien spacecraft
[00:19.780 --> 00:23.700]  push against the vacuum of space as if it were water or air.
[00:23.700 --> 00:27.180]  Let's consider this gyroscope as a teaching lesson.
[00:27.180 --> 00:31.300]  When we put the gyroscope on its side, when it's not spinning, it can spin very easily
[00:31.300 --> 00:33.780]  about its horizontal axis.
[00:33.780 --> 00:39.260]  But then when we give it some spin like that, it can't spin at all about its horizontal
[00:39.260 --> 00:40.660]  axis.
[00:40.660 --> 00:47.300]  So we've created a water-like medium in the vacuum that can be pushed, pushed, pushed.
[00:47.300 --> 00:53.600]  Now suppose we vertically, it can spin quite easily about the vertical axis not spinning.
[00:57.900 --> 01:02.060]  That's what you expect if say this gyroscope was spinning in water.
[01:02.060 --> 01:06.300]  If we spin the other way, it can't spin, it just resists.
[01:06.300 --> 01:11.740]  So it's like there's a vortex around the gyroscope that only allows it to spin one way.
[01:11.740 --> 01:13.740]  Let's put it back on its side again.
[01:13.740 --> 01:17.260]  It can spin about its horizontal axis when it's not spinning.
[01:17.260 --> 01:18.420]  There's no vortex.
[01:18.420 --> 01:23.820]  We create this big vortex in the water like this and then it can't spin.
[01:23.820 --> 01:30.620]  So thus we can turn the vacuum of space into a medium that we can push against using
[01:30.620 --> 01:38.680]  some sophisticated mechanism like for an airplane or boat propeller.
[01:53.820 --> 02:00.340]  If we turn it vertically, we can again spin it through the top, in the direction of spin
[02:00.340 --> 02:23.620]  and stand behind theИ.
[02:23.620 --> 02:26.620]  people might work on it and we could go to the stars.
[02:26.620 --> 02:31.620]  Thank you very much. Please study and show this to people who can't understand.
