[00:00.000 --> 00:03.000]  Look at that.
[00:03.000 --> 00:08.000]  What a beautiful flower wheel.
[00:08.000 --> 00:12.000]  All the magnets are the same.
[00:12.000 --> 00:18.000]  It's fitting opposite the rotating magnetic field.
[00:18.000 --> 00:24.000]  So given any set of magnets like those of the rotating field going clockwise
[00:24.000 --> 00:27.000]  with these coils, wire and series,
[00:27.000 --> 00:30.000]  by changing the polarity of magnets on the top,
[00:30.000 --> 00:34.000]  we can make the rotor be either clockwise with the field or against it
[00:34.000 --> 00:36.000]  and the coils don't get hot.
[00:36.000 --> 00:39.000]  We need about 10 ohms in each coil for good power.
